the alligator's heart because, in effect, it

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:06.620
can bypass its own arteries, mimic this remarkable feat, and we could surely save more human hearts.

00:27:14.380 --> 00:27:18.280
The crocodilians, in fact, appear to have the world's most advanced hearts.

00:27:19.470 --> 00:27:24.810
They've been a zoological mystery for over a century, but now, at last, we're beginning

00:27:24.810 --> 00:27:26.770
to discover their amazing secrets.

00:27:35.790 --> 00:27:38.910
Like our own hearts, an alligator's is split down the middle.

00:27:40.420 --> 00:27:43.960
One side pumps blood to the lungs where it picks up fresh oxygen.

00:27:45.140 --> 00:27:49.490
The other side receives the oxygenated blood and sends it round the body.

00:27:50.320 --> 00:27:51.360
So far, so good.

00:27:52.190 --> 00:27:55.830
The trick comes when the gator dives and can't refill its lungs.

00:27:56.580 --> 00:27:59.970
